## Planning Inputs

### Assumptions

- GCP project `boutique-gke` exists with billing enabled
- Domain `biroltilki.art` DNS manageable (Cloud DNS or delegatable)
- GitHub repo `boutique-gke-sre` with Actions enabled
- PagerDuty account available for integration testing
- User executes all provisioning; AI generates artifacts and guides

### Constraints

- One cluster only; no environment-per-cluster split
- WIF for CI — no long-lived GCP service account keys in GitHub
- Prod-style manual Argo CD sync (even for single cluster)
- Private GKE nodes; ingress via load balancer + static IP

### Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| Cost overrun from always-on cluster | Teardown guide; right-size node pools; autoscaling |
| Binary Auth blocks valid deploys | Document attestor setup; test in Phase 3 before Phase 5 |
| Kyverno blocks Boutique manifests | Policy test in CI; fix Helm values before sync |
| Alert fatigue | Multi-window burn rates; SEV-based routing |
| State lock / Terraform drift | GCS backend; `terraform plan` in CI |

### Dependencies

- GCP APIs enabled (Container, Compute, DNS, IAM, AR, Secret Manager, Monitoring)
- GitHub OIDC → WIF pool/provider configured (Phase 3)
- Argo CD + platform policies before app deploy (Phase 4 → 5)
- Observability stack before SLO definition (Phase 6 before Phase 7)

### Technology Stack

- **GCP:** GKE, Cloud DNS, Cloud Monitoring, Cloud Logging, Managed Prometheus, Cloud Trace, Artifact Registry, WIF, Secret Manager, Binary Authorization, Workload Identity, Cloud Armor, GKE Backup/Velero
- **K8s platform:** Argo CD, Helm, Kyverno, ESO, NetworkPolicy, Prometheus/Grafana, OTel, PDBs, HPA, Cluster Autoscaler
- **Tooling:** Terraform, GitHub Actions, Trivy, cosign, PagerDuty, pre-commit, gitleaks

### High-Level Architecture

Git is the source of truth. GitHub Actions authenticates via WIF, builds container images, scans with Trivy, signs with cosign, and pushes digests to Artifact Registry. Manifests in Git reference digests only. Argo CD syncs to a single private GKE cluster where Kyverno, ESO, and NetworkPolicy enforce policy at admission and runtime. Traffic enters via HTTPS (Google-managed TLS, Cloud Armor, static IP) to Online Boutique and Argo CD. OpenTelemetry exports traces and metrics to Cloud Trace and Managed Prometheus; Grafana provides dashboards. Cloud Monitoring SLOs and burn-rate alerts route to PagerDuty with runbook links.

### Repository Organization

```
boutique-gke-sre/
├── terraform/           # VPC, GKE, DNS, IAM, WIF, monitoring resources
├── gitops/              # Argo CD apps, Helm values, Kyverno, ESO, NetworkPolicy
├── observability/       # OTel, Prometheus, Grafana, SLO/alert definitions
├── docs/
│   ├── setup/           # Topic guides (bootstrap → teardown)
│   └── sre/             # Runbooks, SLOs, on-call, game-days, postmortems
├── scripts/             # Game-day, validation, backup helpers (not setup replacements)
└── .github/workflows/   # CI: WIF, Trivy, cosign, terraform validate
```

