## Implementation Phases

### Phase 1: Repo Scaffold + Terraform Foundation — **S**

**Objectives:** Establish repo structure, tooling, and Terraform base with remote state.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Create folder tree (`terraform/`, `gitops/`, `observability/`, `docs/`, `scripts/`, `.github/`)
- [ ] Add README, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, Makefile, CODEOWNERS
- [ ] Terraform: GCS backend config, provider, project APIs module
- [ ] Terraform: VPC, subnets, Cloud NAT, firewall baseline
- [ ] `docs/setup/01-gcp-project-apis.md`, `02-terraform-remote-state.md`, `03-vpc-nat.md`

**Expected outputs:** Repo scaffold; `terraform/` with VPC module; GCS state bucket; `make validate` passes

**Validation:**
```bash
make validate
cd terraform && terraform init && terraform plan
gcloud storage ls gs://boutique-gke-tfstate  # or configured bucket name
```

---

### Phase 2: GKE Cluster + DNS + Ingress + TLS — **L**

**Objectives:** Provision private GKE cluster with ingress foundation and public HTTPS hostnames.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Terraform: private GKE cluster, node pools, Workload Identity
- [ ] Static IP, Cloud DNS zones/records for `boutique` and `argocd` subdomains
- [ ] Ingress controller (GCE), Google-managed TLS certs
- [ ] Cloud Armor deferred to topic 15 (Phase 7)
- [ ] `docs/setup/04-gke-cluster.md`, `05-cloud-dns.md`, `06-ingress-tls.md`

**Expected outputs:** Running private GKE cluster; DNS A records; TLS cert resources provisioned

**Validation:**
```bash
gcloud container clusters get-credentials boutique-gke --region <region>
kubectl get nodes
dig boutique.biroltilki.art +short
dig argocd.boutique.biroltilki.art +short
```

---

### Phase 3: WIF, Artifact Registry, CI Pipeline Skeleton — **M**

**Objectives:** Secure CI authentication and image supply chain foundation.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Terraform: Artifact Registry repo, WIF pool/provider, CI service account + IAM
- [ ] GitHub Actions: WIF auth, build workflow, Trivy scan (fail critical/high)
- [ ] Push to AR with digest recorded; cosign sign + attest workflow
- [ ] Binary Authorization policy (document attestor requirements)
- [ ] `docs/setup/07-github-wif.md`, `08-artifact-registry-binary-auth.md`

**Expected outputs:** AR repository; WIF working from GitHub Actions; sample image signed in AR

**Validation:**
```bash
gcloud artifacts docker images list <region>-docker.pkg.dev/boutique-gke/...
# GitHub Actions run: build + Trivy + push + cosign green
cosign verify --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com <image>
```

---

### Phase 4: Argo CD + Policies + ESO + NetworkPolicy — **L** ⚠️ REQUIRED GATE

**Objectives:** GitOps control plane and platform security policies before any production workload.

**Tasks:**
- [ ] Bootstrap Argo CD; expose at `argocd.boutique.biroltilki.art` (HTTPS)
- [ ] Deploy Kyverno + 5 minimum policies (digest, probes, resources, netpol labels, no plain Secrets)
- [ ] Deploy External Secrets Operator + Secret Manager integration
- [ ] Default-deny NetworkPolicy with explicit allow rules
- [ ] Policy tests in CI (`tests/` or conftest)
- [ ] `docs/setup/09-argocd-bootstrap.md`, `10-external-secrets.md`, `11-kyverno-policies.md`

**Expected outputs:** Argo CD UI on HTTPS; Kyverno/ESO/NetworkPolicy healthy; policy tests pass

**Validation:**
```bash
curl -I https://argocd.boutique.biroltilki.art
kubectl get pods -n argocd
kubectl get clusterpolicy
kubectl apply -f gitops/policies/test/fixtures/bad-latest.yaml  # expect deny
kubectl get externalsecrets -A
```

**Gate:** Do not proceed to Phase 5 until Phase 4 validation passes.

